\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:Pn-original}{{1}{3}{The product \(P(n)\) itself, with sign, for \(3\le n\le 35\). Composite \(n\) give the exact value \(0\); prime \(n\) give a nonzero value of rapidly decreasing magnitude and no fixed sign pattern. The exponential decay rate is quantified in Theorem~\ref {thm:prime-third-scale}}{figure.caption.2}{}}
